Root cause: vehicle.state on the Vehicle type exists in TypeScript interfaces but the
/api/v1/vehicles list endpoint does NOT return a meaningful state field (it returns empty
or stale data). The FSM state is only in VehicleState.state from /vehicles/{id}/state.


=== REASONING ===
The Vehicle type has a state field in the TypeScript interface, but the /vehicles list
endpoint returns stale/empty state. The actual FSM state (parked, driving, charging, etc.)
is only available from /vehicles/{id}/state which returns VehicleState with a state field.

All deriveStatus/getVehicleStatus functions were reading v.state (Vehicle.state) which is
undefined/stale, causing them to always fall through to 'offline'. They need to read from
VehicleState.state instead (s?.state, state?.state).

Pages that display vehicle.state directly (QuickStatsPage, GlancePage) needed to either
fetch useVehicleState or use the already-fetched stateData.

=== CHANGES ===
1. useVehicles.ts: getVehicleStatus — read state?.state instead of v.state; added parked→online mapping
2. helpers.ts: deriveStatus — same fix as above
3. VehicleHeroCardWidget.tsx: lines 70,77 — status={state?.state ?? 'offline'} instead of vehicle.state
4. VehicleHero.tsx: line 35 — status from state?.state; line 65 — status check; line 190 — s.state check
5. VehicleHero.tsx: buildStatCards vehicle param → _vehicle (now unused)
6. QuickStatsPage.tsx: added useVehicleState import + hook call; display stateData?.state?.state
7. GlancePage.tsx: isOnline from state?.state; badge text from state?.state
8. VehicleListPage.tsx: local deriveStatus — same fix pattern

